 "response": {
  "text": "For **oily skin**, I’d prioritize a cleanser that removes excess oil without leaving your face tight or stripped. If you also get blackheads/pimples, salicylic acid is particularly useful because it helps unclog pores. [www.ndtvshopping.com](https://www.ndtvshopping.com/beauty-and-grooming/best-salicylic-acid-face-washes-for-acne-prone-skin-in-monsoon-11662605?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n### My picks under ₹500\n\n### [The Derma Co Sali-Cinamide Anti-Acne Face Wash]()\n*₹232*\n\n### [Chemist At Play Oil & Acne Control Face Wash]()\n*₹254*\n\n### [Simple Kind to Skin Refreshing Facial Gel Wash]()\n*₹204*\n\n### [Dot & Key Cica Calming Blemish Clearing Face Wash]()\n*₹214*\n\n### [Be Bodywise 2% Salicylic Acid Face Wash]()\n*₹284*\n\n**🥇 Best overall: The Derma Co Sali-Cinamide 2% Salicylic Acid + 2% Niacinamide** — currently around **₹232–₹224** in the shopping results. Good choice if you're oily **and prone to acne/blackheads**. [www.purplle.com](https://www.purplle.com/collections/salicylic-acid-face-wash-for-oily-skin?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n**🥈 If you have oily + sensitive skin:** **Simple Kind to Skin Refreshing Facial Gel Wash** — a gentler option; choose this if salicylic-acid cleansers tend to make your skin dry or irritated.\n\n**🥉 If oil + acne are your main concerns:** **Chemist At Play Oil & Acne Control** — around **₹254**, with a strong current rating in the shopping results.\n\n**My simple recommendation:**  \n- **Very oily + pimples/blackheads → The Derma Co Sali-Cinamide**\n- **Oily but sensitive → Simple Refreshing**\n- **Oily without much acne → a gentle cleanser rather than 2% salicylic acid every wash**\n\nIf you tell me **your age + whether you have acne/blackheads + whether your skin is sensitive**, I can narrow it down to **one exact face wash** for you.",
